## HTTP tools

`http_get`, `http_post`, and `http_head` connect directly to public HTTPS
endpoints. Environment proxy settings are not used. Private, loopback,
link-local, metadata, and reserved addresses are rejected, including mapped
IPv6 addresses and DNS answers that mix public and blocked addresses. DNS
addresses are checked by the connection resolver, and each request uses its
own connection agent.

URL credentials and caller `Host` header overrides are rejected. Other
request headers are supported. Redirects are returned without following
the destination. The timeout accepts 1–120 seconds and remains active
through DNS resolution, connection setup, and response body consumption.

GET and POST return the first 10,000 characters of the response text. GET's
`contentLength` reports the full response's character count; HEAD's
`contentLength` reports the server's header value or `unknown`.
